{"id": "EUVD-2026-81870", "enisaUuid": "a612cb13-e4cc-363c-b4a3-13a1d1ee7a7b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/md-llbitmap: prevent create failure bitmap UAF\n\nllbitmap_create() publishes mddev->bitmap before reading the bitmap\nsuperblock. This is needed because llbitmap_read_sb() can initialize a\nnew bitmap and flush it through helpers that use mddev->bitmap.\n\nIf llbitmap_read_sb() fails, the old cleanup dropped bitmap_info.mutex\nand freed llbitmap before clearing mddev->bitmap. Readers such as\n/proc/mdstat rely on bitmap_info.mutex to keep the bitmap pointer stable\nwhile collecting bitmap stats, so they could observe the stale pointer\nafter the failed create path released the mutex.\n\nClear mddev->bitmap while still holding bitmap_info.mutex, then free the\nfailed llbitmap after dropping the mutex. This makes mutex-protected\nreaders see either a live bitmap or no bitmap.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/930cc4f1af5a1afcd545a6ba00e38921ff8401e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f0722435ce3a844dbb66b9bb0a18229dcc8739c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2116c2f0a0e547615886900e2ed8c529c016499b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90277", "GHSA-x88w-2pq9-75r8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "33097446-b9d2-3c96-b4e3-048ddd3aeb3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3828750a-02d7-3527-bb76-103a83978fc4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4227a051-43bc-355b-b80a-64a17fac3ccd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <2f0722435ce3a844dbb66b9bb0a18229dcc8739c"}, {"id": "4a0a9bcc-b7f5-3811-9e5a-27102adb094b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <2116c2f0a0e547615886900e2ed8c529c016499b"}, {"id": "b8f5a052-247f-3afa-8e0e-211654a8b5f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "bf297a63-e562-3fd8-b166-10cfb38a13da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5ab829f1971dc99f2aac10846c378e67fc875abc <930cc4f1af5a1afcd545a6ba00e38921ff8401e0"}, {"id": "e1663105-02f5-3cb6-832c-bbc8e3644e28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "f08790b4-a841-3373-8326-a006a1a1cb62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5374cfe5-e83e-3dac-868e-83244d55e7f4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}